{#
  /happy-hour/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  This page earns 1,361 clicks with almost no internal links pointing at it. It
  catches 1,107 happy-hour clicks across 165 queries; all six location pages
  combined catch 32, because "tajima happy hour" contains no location and a
  location page cannot answer it.

  East Village leads. Its ARP for `happy hour near me` in the map pack is 1.00
  against 12 to 14 everywhere else, and the brief says lead with it. The order
  here is happyHour.json's order, and East Village is first in that file.

  ============================ TIMES AND PRICES ARE PULLED ============================

  This page once rendered per-location windows and drink and food prices, all
  carried from the design concept. They were removed on Steve's call, for the
  same reason opening hours stayed off every other page: a happy hour window is
  the same promise as an opening hour, and the failure mode is someone driving
  over at 5 for a window that shut at 4. Prices were worse: CLAUDE.md says menu
  prices are never published without client approval.

  The windows, drinks and food markup is still below behind an `if`. Put real
  values from Amanda into _data/happyHour.json and it renders again with no
  template change. Do not restore the concept values.

  Operating hours and happy hour windows are DIFFERENT DATA. Connor confirmed
  operating hours on 2026-09-09 and they are published on the location pages.
  Happy hour windows remain unconfirmed everywhere and nothing here implies
  otherwise.

  ============================ WHAT IS NEW HERE ============================

  REDESIGNED 2026-09-09. The page was an honest table of "being confirmed" and
  nothing else, so a reader who arrived from "tajima happy hour" learned only
  that we could not answer them. It now answers the question underneath that
  one, which we can answer: what each room actually pours. Every line traces to
  CLIENT_FACTS.md and lives in _data/happyHour.json with its source recorded.

  THE PAGE 18 DEVICES, and they are scoped to this page. The October 2025 brand
  guidelines, Section 5.1 Digital Application, show the promotional treatment:
  a black header band, Sesame Gold running as a full-bleed field with black
  type, thin full-bleed red stripes between bands, the starburst badge in red
  with a white stroke and white brush type, and a red field carrying the
  ghosted line-art pattern. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md now records that gold as a field
  is permitted in promotional applications, citing that page, and that this is
  the only route that gets it.

  THE GUIDELINES' CONTENT IS NOT IN SCOPE AND THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL. That
  artifact features North Park, which is closed, Tijuana as a peer location,
  Carnitas Ramen with a hero photograph, "ALL SLURPS WELCOME", which is retired
  voice, and "Authentic Japanese roots", which is banned copy. Colour, field
  and badge treatment only.

  IMAGERY, AND A CORRECTION. This comment used to say "there is no unused local
  photograph of a drink, a bar, or a happy hour plate". THAT WAS WRONG. Six
  exist: three Convoy house mixed drinks and three Convoy margaritas, all
  1280x853, all sitting in photos.json with the generator's draft alt. The
  claim was written from the curated sets in roomPhotos.js rather than from the
  manifest itself, which is the difference between "nobody has selected one"
  and "none exists". PHOTO_AUDIT.md caught it.

  All six now have reviewed alt. ONE is placed, on Convoy's card, because all
  six are Convoy photographs and photos.json's _rule is that a photograph
  reaches a location's surface only if its filename names that location. The
  other five rooms render no photo rather than borrowing Convoy's, which is the
  same rule the location galleries follow and the same reason the mega-menu
  shows one deliberately generic dish rather than two real rooms and four
  holding slots.

  So one card of six carries a photograph. That is a true picture of what we
  have, not a design choice, and it resolves the day another room is shot.
  What this page still needs is the documentary shoot, DESIGN_SYSTEM.md open
  item 3.

  NO STANDALONE ICONS ON THE ROOM CARDS. Happy hour wants a glass, a bottle or
  a tap and the sprite has twelve marks, all of them food or the wordmark.
  DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's rule is that where no icon matches the subject, the
  heading takes none. The one place a mark genuinely matches is Plaza Bonita,
  whose answer is that the bowls are the same bowls.
#}
{%- set spriteIcons = ["ramen-bowl", "chopsticks-noodles"] %}
{% include "components/icon-sprite.njk" %}

{# ==================== 1. THE BLACK BAND ==================== #}
{#
  Page 18's header device. The site header sits above it carrying the mark and
  the wordmark, so this band carries the page title rather than repeating the
  logo underneath itself.
#}
<section class="hh-band" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="hh-band__inner">
    <h1 class="hh-band__title" id="page-title">Happy Hour</h1>
    <p class="hh-band__sub">
      Six rooms in San Diego, and not one of them pours the same list. Here is what is behind each bar, and how to find out what is running today.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="hh-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{# ==================== 2. THE GOLD FIELD ==================== #}
{#
  The one full-bleed Sesame Gold field in the build, and the reason the page
  exists beyond the times. Black type on gold measures 8.4 to 1.

  Full-bleed colour fields stay sharp: no radius here. Cards take the radius
  scale, fields do not.

  Every room line is happyHour.json's `bar` field, which carries its own
  `_barSource` recording where in CLIENT_FACTS.md it comes from.
#}
<section class="hh-gold" aria-labelledby="what-title">
  {%- set burstTop = "Open" %}
  {%- set burstBottom = "Daily" %}
  {% include "components/starburst.njk" %}

  {#
    Page 18's other gold-field device: a red line-art mark drawn large and
    bleeding off the edge of the band. This is a field ornament, not a
    standalone mark, so the one-icon-per-heading rule does not apply to it and
    it carries no meaning: it is aria-hidden and the copy does not depend on
    it. Chopsticks lifting noodles, because that is the mark whose silhouette
    survives being cropped by the band edge.
  #}
  <span class="hh-gold__artwrap" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="hh-gold__art"><svg><use href="#i-chopsticks-noodles"></use></svg></span>
  </span>

  <div class="hh-gold__inner">
    <h2 class="hh-gold__title" id="what-title">What happy hour is <em>here.</em></h2>

    <div class="hh-gold__body">
      <p class="hh-gold__para">
        Tajima is not a chain with one bar programme printed six times. Mercury has the full bar, with craft cocktails, Japanese whisky and a wine list. College Heights has the largest beer program of the seven. Convoy has the deepest izakaya list to drink alongside. Crown Point pours local craft and a matcha-forward list for anyone not drinking. East Village has six taps and the walk to Petco Park. Plaza Bonita is quick-serve inside the mall and serves no alcohol at all.
      </p>
      <p class="hh-gold__para">
        The windows are not the same either, and we are confirming them room by room rather than printing a time the door does not honor. Until they are up here, every room's number is below and they will tell you what is running today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="hh-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{# ==================== 3. THE ROOMS ==================== #}
{#
  Cards, not a table. Adapted from the .hh-card block that had been sitting
  dead in happy-hour.css since the flat table replaced it, including its
  --plaza modifier, rather than inventing a third treatment for the same job.

  THE THREE-WAY BRANCH IS UNCHANGED AND DELIBERATE. A room renders as no
  alcohol, as confirmed windows, or as pending with a phone number. The
  windows, drinks and food markup is intact, so real values from Amanda render
  here with no template change.

  What changed is that a pending room is no longer a card that only says
  "being confirmed". It says what that room pours, which is confirmed, and
  then says the window is not, which is honest without being empty.
#}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="rooms-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="rooms-title">Six rooms, six <em>bars.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        What each one pours is confirmed. What time it starts is not, yet. Tap a number and ask.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="hh-grid">
      {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
      {%- set loc = (locations.items | where("id", hh.id)) | first %}
      {%- set roomDrinks = roomPhotos[hh.id].drinks %}
      <article class="hh-card{% if hh.noAlcohol %} hh-card--plaza{% endif %} reveal">
        {#- Renders only for a room with its own drinks photography, which is
            Convoy alone. See roomPhotos.js. -#}
        {%- if roomDrinks %}
        {%- set shot = roomDrinks | first %}
        <figure class="hh-card__photo">
          <img src="{{ shot.src }}" alt="{{ shot.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ shot.width }}" height="{{ shot.height }}">
          <figcaption>{{ shot.caption }}</figcaption>
        </figure>
        {%- endif %}
        <h3 class="hh-card__name"><a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ hh.name }}</a></h3>
        <p class="hh-card__tag">{{ hh.tag }}</p>

        {%- if hh.noAlcohol %}
        {#
          Plaza Bonita reads as a deliberate answer, not an omission. The mark
          is the one on this page that matches its subject: the point of this
          card is that the bowls are the same bowls.

          "No happy hour at all" is gone. That phrasing is not in
          CLIENT_FACTS.md and the room's own live Toast catalog carries a
          priced Happy Hours section, so the two contradict each other and the
          negative was the one we were publishing. See _plazaReconciliation in
          happyHour.json. What is published is the confirmed fact: no alcohol.
        #}
        <span class="mark mark--lg mark--disc hh-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#i-ramen-bowl"></use></svg></span>
        <p class="hh-card__bar">{{ hh.bar }}</p>
        <p class="hh-card__note">Nothing is discounted here because nothing is poured here. Come for the bowl.</p>
        {%- else %}
        <p class="hh-card__bar">{{ hh.bar }}</p>

        {%- if hh.windows | length %}
        {# Renders only when happyHour.json holds confirmed values. #}
        <div class="hh-card__hours">
          {%- for window in hh.windows %}
          <div class="hh-card__hours-row">
            <span>{{ window.time }}</span>
            <span class="hh-card__hours-days">{{ window.days }}</span>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        {%- if hh.drinks | length or hh.food | length %}
        <div class="hh-card__lists">
          {%- if hh.drinks | length %}
          <div>
            <p class="hh-card__list-label">Drinks</p>
            <ul class="hh-card__list">
              {%- for item in hh.drinks %}<li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if hh.food | length %}
          <div>
            <p class="hh-card__list-label">Food</p>
            <ul class="hh-card__list">
              {%- for item in hh.food %}<li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- else %}
        <p class="hh-card__pending">The window here is being confirmed.</p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- endif %}

        {#
          Every card carries the number, Plaza Bonita included. The phone is
          the one value on this page we are certain of, and a room's number is
          never the wrong thing to hand someone standing on a street corner.
          It sits outside the three-way branch so it cannot go missing from a
          state nobody thought to check.
        #}
        <a class="hh-card__phone" href="{{ loc.phone | telHref }}">
          {{ loc.phone }}
          <span class="u-visually-hidden">, call {{ hh.name }}</span>
        </a>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

